# Implementation Plan - Phase E: Tropical Cyclone Reliability Specialist (Gate 4 / P1)

Phase E implements the **Tropical Cyclone Reliability Specialist (`CYCLONE_RELIABILITY_V1`)**, diagnosing medium-range NWP cyclone forecast failure without collapsing it into one opaque score. It explicitly decomposes cyclone forecast reliability into:
1. **Track error threshold exceedance** (position error $> 100$ km at 48h, $> 180$ km at 72h)
2. **Intensity error threshold exceedance** ($> 15$ knots / $7.7$ m/s)
3. **Rapid Intensification (RI) failure** (failure to predict $\ge 30$ kt / 24h deepening or false alarm)
4. **Landfall location error** (displacement $> 80$ km)
5. **Landfall timing error** (arrival offset $> 6$ hours)
6. **Track uncertainty & conformal uncertainty radius** (situation-dependent calibrated uncertainty bounds)

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Decomposed Failure Modes**: Cyclone reliability will NOT be collapsed into one opaque score. Track, intensity, rapid intensification, landfall timing, and landfall position are independently predicted and reported.
> - **Anti-Leakage & Ocean Variables**: Strictly issue-time features at $t_0$. No post-valid-time best-track observations (IMD / JTWC) or unavailable deep-ocean thermal fields enter issue-time inference.
> - **Strict Null Safety**: Landfall outputs are strictly `null` if the cyclone is not forecast to make landfall or if coastal proximity is unsupported.

